{"name":"Epidote Olvene Ore","hex":"#ab924b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"epidote","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a class of mixed calcium iron aluminium sorosilicates found in metamorphic rocks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidote"},{"term":"ore","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Orejón."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock or other material that contains valuable or utilitarian materials; primarily a rock containing metals or gems for which it is typically mined and processed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Epidote","blocks":[{"text":"Epidote is a calcium aluminium iron sorosilicate mineral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/%D0%AD%D0%BF%D0%B8%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%82%28%D0%BF%D1%83%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82%29.jpg/330px-%D0%AD%D0%BF%D0%B8%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%82%28%D0%BF%D1%83%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epidote","wikidata":"Q272844"},{"title":"Ore","blocks":[{"text":"Ore is natural rock or sediment that contains one or more valuable minerals, typically including metals, concentrated above background levels, and that is economically viable to mine and process. Ore grade refers to the concentration of the desired material it contains. The value of the metals or minerals a rock contains must be weighed against the cost of extraction to determine whether it is of sufficiently high grade to be worth mining and is therefore considered an ore. A complex ore is one containing more than one valuable mineral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Banded_iron_formation.png/330px-Banded_iron_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ore","wikidata":"Q1027